## Structured English SRD data

- Source: [bankenichi/5etools-srd at commit `3b26955ea5394fde43a1e33b2a878b42cebbe51c`](https://github.com/bankenichi/5etools-srd/tree/3b26955ea5394fde43a1e33b2a878b42cebbe51c), files `data/bestiary/bestiary-srd521.json` and `data/conditionsdiseases.json`.
- The source repository identifies this content as SRD 5.2.1, CC BY 4.0, and provides the required Wizards of the Coast attribution in its `ATTRIBUTION.md`.

## Russian translations

- Monster names and stat blocks: Petr Radilov (OmnisGM), CC BY 4.0. Imported from [my-git-store/nastolka-dnd-reference at commit `547fc77f31649f69ff67c97699125d491f2f9209`](https://github.com/my-git-store/nastolka-dnd-reference/tree/547fc77f31649f69ff67c97699125d491f2f9209).
- Conditions, items/equipment, spells, feats, backgrounds, and species: Petr Radilov (OmnisGM), CC BY 4.0. Source: [OmnisGM-App/OmnisGM-Rules at commit `1f7192be159e84f2db7212565866747094e3b9de`](https://github.com/OmnisGM-App/OmnisGM-Rules/tree/1f7192be159e84f2db7212565866747094e3b9de/src/dnd/srd-5.2/ru); the source repository's SRD 5.2.1 `LICENSE-RU.md` identifies the translation terms. Some item records have no exact Russian source section; for those records, RU description is empty and the English name is a fallback, not a Russian translation.

Translation texts are redistributed under CC BY 4.0 as indicated by the respective source repositories; license text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

## Changes made in this repository

The SRD source data is included in this API's JSON catalog with complete original structures retained under `mechanics.source_data`. Russian text is attached only where an exact source heading/name match was found. `status: source` means the text is sourced and attributed; it does not imply independent proofreading. 170 item/equipment records (137 `item`, 33 `equipment`) have no matched Russian description and retain the English name as a fallback with an empty description and no translation status.

